From 636a846c75fa4208f400fc00692ae963bc5cdf0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:28:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: Back that clears tab search returns the sheet to its
 stop

Opening tab search takes the sheet to full. The Back press (or the
clear button) that collapses the field now returns the sheet to the stop
it had when the search opened: a sheet that was at half animates back to
half; a sheet the user had already opened to full stays full. Hiding the
keyboard and emptying the text without collapsing do not move the sheet,
and the 3-step Back order (keyboard, clear, close) is unchanged.

When the clear also snaps the sheet, the search row's fade transition is
skipped; the settle cut it off and left the actions row half faded.
---
 .../browser/bare/BareVerticalTabsDrawer.java  |  72 ++++++++++-
 .../bare/BareVerticalTabsDrawerUnitTest.java  | 117 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 186 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/bare/BareVerticalTabsDrawer.java b/chrome/android/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/bare/BareVerticalTabsDrawer.java
